// endpoint_watch_feed.proto — WatchFeed: one feed's live tail. FEED section.
// ONE connection per OPEN feed — the root feed while the workspace view is
// up, plus one per expanded subagent bubble — so THE CONNECTION IS THE
// PLACEMENT: every row on a stream belongs to the feed its token named, and
// no frame carries a feed address. History is OpenFeed's page and
// GetFeedPage's walk; this stream is what changes NOW.
//
// THE STREAM IS STANDING: it spans turns (a turn's end arrives as the
// FeedTurnEnded ROW, never as this stream concluding), and it ends only when
// the client cancels it (collapsing a bubble, closing the view). A stream
// ending any other way is a TRANSPORT FAILURE — re-entered by re-opening the
// feed — which is exactly what keeps a dropped pipe distinguishable from
// every real ending. Views only ride streams — there is no keepalive frame,
// and a refused open closes the stream at the transport.

